### Creating Site-to-Site VPN :


#### Configuration on Head office sophos :
- Login sophos firewall
- Go to site-to-site vpn
- Under IPsec
- Click on Add
- Give Office name (for example : BranchOffice)
- Uncheck Create firewall rule
- Connection type : site-to-site
- Gateway type : Respond only
- Under Encryption : Profile -> DefaultHeadOffice -> Authentication type -> Preshared key (Enter your key , this same key should define in same branchoffice).
- On same page Under Gateway settings : Local gateway -> Listening interface -> select WAN port IP ->  , Remote gateway -> Gateway address -> branchoffice static ip
- In local subnet -> Add new item -> Enter the details of (Headoffice subnet) type:network ip address details
- In remote subnet -> Add new item -> enter the details of (Branchoffice subnet) type:network ip address details
- Now Save
- Now we have to create the rule 1. LAN to VPN (local subnet of headoffice communicate with branchoffice subnet) 2. VPN to LAN (Branchoffice subnet communicate with headoffice subnet)
- Now go to rules and policies -> Firewall rules -> Add firewall rule -> New firewall rule
- give rule name "Lan-VPN" , Rule position : TOP , Action : Accept , Rule group : None , Tick : log firewall traffic
- Under Source -> Source zones : tick LAN , Source network and devicess : Any , During scheduled time : All the time
- Under Destination and services -> Destination zones : tick VPN , Destination networks : Any , Services : Any
- Now Save
- Now add firewall rule -> new firewall rule (for VPN-to-LAN)
- Rule Name : VPN-to-LAN , Rule position : Top , Rule Group : None , Action : Accept , Tick : log firewal traffic
- Under Source , Sources zone -> Tick VPN , Source networks and devices  -> any , During Scheduled time : All the time
- Under Destination and services , Destination zones : LAN , Destination networks : ANy , Services : any
- on same page click on "create linked NAT rule" create NAT rule
- Translated source (SNAT) -> MASQ then save 
- then save the rule
- Now main sophos page go the Administration -> Device access -> On Wan section enable Ping/Ping6 check -> IPsec check
- VPN section check the same as LAN section


### Configuration on Branch office subnet
- Sophos login
- Go to site to site VPN section
- Name : HO , IP version select IPv4 , uncheck create firewall rule
- Gateway type : Initiate the connection
- Under Encryption : Profile -> DefaultBranchOffice -> Authentication type -> Preshared key (Enter your key , this same key should define in same headoffice).
- On same page Under Gateway settings : Local gateway -> Listening interface -> select WAN port IP ->  , Remote gateway -> Gateway address -> headoffice static ip
- In local subnet -> Add new item -> Enter the details of (Branchoffice subnet) type:network ip address details
- In remote subnet -> Add new item -> enter the details of (Headoffice subnet) type:network ip address details
- Now Save
- Now go to rules and policies -> Firewall rules -> Add firewall rule -> New firewall rule
- give rule name "Lan-VPN" , Rule position : TOP , Action : Accept , Rule group : None , Tick : log firewall traffic
- Under Source -> Source zones : tick LAN , Source network and devicess : Any , During scheduled time : All the time
- Under Destination and services -> Destination zones : tick VPN , Destination networks : Any , Services : Any
- save the rule
- Create another firwall rule , Rule name : "VPN-LAN" , Rule position : TOP , Rule group : None
- Under Source -> Source zones : tick VPN , Source network and devicess : Any , During scheduled time : All the time
- Under Destination and services , Destination zones : LAN , Destination networks : ANy , Services : any
- on same page click on "create linked NAT rule" create NAT rule
- Translated source (SNAT) -> MASQ then save 
- then save the rule
- Now main sophos page go the Administration -> Device access -> On Wan section enable Ping/Ping6 check -> IPsec check (if no available not problem)
- VPN section check the same as LAN section





















